    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI want the text being commented to also be yanked.\r\n\r\nMost often it's one or more lines of code that I plan to comment out, then paste and modify.\r\nThis could be an `option` or setup in `hooks`.\r\nI've able to accomplish the same with other plugins, but only because of specific functions they provide.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n```lua\r\n    \"numToStr/Comment.nvim\",\r\n    opts = {\r\n      pre_hook = function(ctx)\r\n        local lines = require(\"Comment.utils\").get_lines(ctx.range)\r\n        vim.fn.setreg(\"+\", lines)\r\n      end,\r\n    },\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2024-02-16T14:33:15Z",
