            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nHaving hooks take some context data seems reasonable enough to add, so it now should be in `main` branch.\r\n\r\nHere is a [list of fields](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/14dee9cccaea6a5b4d1e085a202752517c02ce82/doc/mini-comment.txt#L142-L146) that hooks now can use. Beware that those same hooks are called both for comment toggling and computing textobject, so `line_start` and `line_end` won't always be present in `pre` hook.\r\n\r\nHere is a snippet which achieves similar goal to the one from original comment:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal yank_lines = function(data)\r\n  if data.action ~= 'toggle' then return end\r\n  local lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(0, data.line_start - 1, data.line_end, false)\r\n  vim.fn.setreg('+', lines)\r\nend\r\nrequire('mini.comment').setup({ hooks = { pre = yank_lines } })\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2024-02-16T14:40:10Z",
